Daenerys Targaryen is known by many  titles and on the latest episode of Game  of Thrones she gains another one a name  she insisted she would never take on as  long as she could help it here's how the  twist went down and what it all means  Daenerys admits she has only known fear  in Westeros not the love that her nephew  boyfriend and potentially rival claimant  to the Iron Throne Jon Snow has come to  receive this realization combined with  her newfound knowledge that her master  of whisperers Varys committed treason  against her and shifting his loyalty to  John Plus the recent death of her  trusted advisor Masson day pushes  Daenerys past her breaking point the  mother of dragons dives headfirst into  the madness that her father the  so-called Mad King suffered when he sat  on the Iron Throne omits Robert's  rebellion in episode 5 Dany became the  mad Queen destroying King's Landing and  killing thousands of innocent men women  and children on her mission to unseat  Cersei Lannister and take the Iron  Throne herself the iron boom  perhaps you should try wanting something  else  Dany time and again has stated that  she's not a carbon copy of her father  and she wouldn't make the same mistakes  he did I am NOT here to be queen of the  ashes but that's exactly what wound up  happening during this latest episode in  a moment many viewers felt was a wild  twist however in the eyes of Game of  Thrones showrunners Daenerys going mad  wasn't exactly a big shock David Benioff  and Dan Weiss explained during the shows  inside the episode featurettes that  Thrones had long for shadow Dany  spiraling into instability and that  there are plenty of clues sprinkled  throughout past seasons that signaled  this dark turn would happen eventually  one such clue is the death of Daenerys  brother Viserys back in season one Danny  didn't second-guess her decision to have  called Drogo pour molten gold over  Viserys head and refused to look away  when the deed was carried out wanting to  watch him suffer through the pain  he is no TRACON  if I cannot kill that dragon Daenerys  has a history of killing or ordering  others to kill on her behalf and  exhibiting no signs of hesitancy or  remorse she burnt a witch alive and  almost relished in her cries she  sentenced people to die in a vault den  didn't think twice Daenerys also burnt a  slave-owner  alive and was thrilled to do it she gave  a chilling speech about how she deserved  to rule just before she burnt a horde of  Dothraki warlords to death and who could  forget her ruthless flaming of Samwell  Tarly 'he's brother and father plus her  execution of varus that came at the top  of this very episode the season has  shown time and time again that Daenerys  isn't afraid of doling out death  sentences and she's been pretty clear  about her intentions from the start we  will take back what was stolen from me  and destroy and those who wronged me we  will lay waste to armies and burn cities  to the ground but that attitude  contrasts harshly with the other side of  her personality the side that frees  wrongfully enslaved people liberate  cities and promises to break the wheel  of oppression instead of simply taking  her own turn as the person in charge  Dany turning into the person she said  she would never become the woman who  strikes fear in the hearts of the  Westeros II people the queen of the  ashes the spitting image of her father  was shocking to behold even if there  were some breadcrumbs leading up to the  snapping point Dan wisest said he  doesn't feel that Daenerys always  intended to burn King's Landing and its  citizens to a crisp though there was a  lot of buildup that would show cause for  her doing so rather Weiss noted that  Dany decided to take that course of  action the moment she arrived in the  capital city it's in that moment on the  walls of King's Landing where she's  looking at that symbol of everything  that was taken from her when she makes  the decision to make this personal  Benioff added that Daenerys may never  have become the Mad Queen if her journey  to the iron throne had played out  differently circumstances have been  different I don't think the side of Dany  ever would have come out if Cersei  hadn't betrayed her if Sir she hadn't  executed me someday if John hadn't told  her the truth  unfortunately this side of Daenerys  Targaryen did come out and it will  probably be her  doing it's tough to imagine the people  of Westeros rallying behind Daenerys  after she needlessly murdered thousands  of people via dragon fire and decimated  the capital now that she's gone full Mad  Queen Dany likely can't go back to the  person she used to be her dream to sit  on the Iron Throne may never come true  despite her greatest enemy Cersei dying  in the chaos of the siege and John  constantly saying he will always support  Danny it will be an intense fight to the  finish during the final episode of Game  of Thrones as Daenerys actors Emilia  Clarke told The Hollywood Reporter it's  the car crash of every emotion you can  possibly imagine it's like a nuclear  bomb check out one of our newest videos  right here plus even more looper videos  about Game of Thrones they're coming  soon subscribe to our YouTube channel  and hit the bell so you don't miss a  single one  [Music]
 

